{"Title":"An Act to continue providing for virtual notarization to address challenges related to COVID-19","BillNumber":"H1540","DocketNumber":"HD1107","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"RMH1","Name":"Richard M. Haggerty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RMH1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T11:01:27.59"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"RMH1","Name":"Richard M. Haggerty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RMH1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T11:01:27.59"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1540/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Haggerty of Woburn, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1540) of Richard M. Haggerty for legislation to further regulate virtual notarization.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 8 of chapter 71 of the acts of 2020 is hereby amended by inserting after the word “emergency” the following words:- or July 31, 2024, whichever is later.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}